 logic inside every RDL recovered, the right target chosen per report, editable PBIP, TMDL and paginated artifacts generated, every report validated against its original.",meta:["Microsoft","SSRS","PBIP / TMDL","Paginated"],href:"/ssrs-to-power-bi-migration",cta:"Open the track"},{title:"To Fabric",desc:"SQL Server, SSIS, ADF and Synapse estates become OneLake: mirrored where a source stays, rebuilt as Fabric pipelines, Warehouse and Lakehouse items where it moves, Direct Lake models under the same reports.",meta:["Microsoft","OneLake","Fabric pipelines","Direct Lake"],href:"/migration-to-fabric",cta:"Open the track"}],d=[{tag:"Gate 01",title:"Intent",desc:"AI reads the estate: packages, procedures, reports, pipelines. What each one is for and what depends on it comes out as a graph, not a guess."},{tag:"Gate 02",title:"Target",desc:"Each object gets a destination: rebuilt, consolidated, served by a model, or retired. An engineer decides; the reason is recorded."},{tag:"Gate 03",title:"Build",desc:"Deterministic generators produce the artifacts, editable and in Git. Nothing opaque, nothing you cannot change."},{tag:"Gate 04",title:"Evidence",desc:"Every object is validated against its original: figures, rows, behaviour. The evidence travels with it."},{tag:"Gate 05",title:"Cutover",desc:"Consumers repointed, the original retired, the runbook handed over. Approved by a person, every time."}];function c(){return(0,t.jsxs)(a.default,{hero:{index:"04",total:"05",eyebrow:"Databricks and Microsoft",lines:["Estate","Migration."],lede:"One method, three destinations. Databricks: Synapse, SSIS and T-SQL estates become the Lakehouse. Microsoft: SSRS reports become Power BI, and SQL Server, SSIS and Synapse estates become OneLake on Fabric. In every case AI recovers intent, deterministic generators produce editable artifacts, and an engineer approves every consequential decision."},sections:n,children:[(0,t.jsxs)(a.Beat,{id:"tracks",index:"01",eyebrow:"Choose the destination",